  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Acidic nature is more, if the stability of the conjugate base is more. Electron withdrawing groups increases the stability. Nitro group at para position shows <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;effect and meta position it shows <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>&nbsp;effect only.</p><p>Methoxy group at meta position shows <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>&nbsp;effect, but effect is Iess than nitro group. Methoxy group at para position shows <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;effect that decreases the acidic nature.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0184_48d0c477d9f1.png\" style=\"width: 440px; height: 188px;\" /></p></blockquote>"
